      "message": "I don\u0027t think we are consistent. I don\u0027t see any recommendations in the C++ style guide or http://go/c-readability-advice.\n\nI try to name things so that it\u0027s \"readable English\". That\u0027s somewhat vague, but basically, I check to see how it reads in conditionals:\n\n```\nif (fp_match_success())\n```\n\n```\nif (is_fp_match_success())\n```\n\n```\nif (fp_match_is_successful())\n```\n\nTo me the first sounds fine. The second one is a bit awkward; maybe `is_fp_match` or `fp_matches` would be better. The third one also sounds ok, but it\u0027s longer without being any clearer, so I\u0027d probably still go with the first.",
